{"ts":"2026-08-22T11:40:19.543Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"stealth/ox-alpha","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"d9a0d530422e5cfffd2e5480","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"stealth/ox-alpha","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-22T11:40:19.543Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-22T11:40:19.543Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Added tests/concurrency_contract.rs: 8 concurrent OS processes each append 3 comments to one shared item using the per-item lock and its configured wait_ms budget (60s in the fixture), with no test-side coordination. Asserts every accepted mutation survives: comment-row count, history record count, and the before_hash/after_hash chain all agree with the 24 successful processes. The test found and fixed a real race: locate_item read the document before lock acquisition, so writers could apply changes to stale bytes; reads now happen inside the critical section for update, comment, and close. Lock-guard sabotage verified: releasing the lock immediately reproduces lost updates and fails the test."}]}],"before_hash":"666f4ec663891fed4681e5b1ffd400d0b11b4c9e4723b961775bdeabc85eb7e3","after_hash":"e9d126f05d741f9e717cd232a127d2e20bac657fee5cc5c9902c070de7a9ce1b","item_hash_version":2,"message":"Multi-process no-lost-update evidence"}
