{"ts":"2026-08-27T20:19:46.699Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"e2d236e796e54a637dde588e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-27T20:19:46.699Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Follow-up audit entry recorded under established ownership (item claimed by pi-agent) to correct the order in which this tracker learned the concurrency-test evidence. Restated evidence: tests/concurrency_contract.rs spawns 8 concurrent OS processes that each append 3 comments to one shared item using the per-item lock and its configured wait_ms budget (60s in the fixture), with no test-side coordination; it asserts every accepted mutation survives (comment-row count, history record count, and the before_hash/after_hash chain all agree with the 24 successful processes). The test found and fixed a real race: locate_item read the document before lock acquisition, so writers could apply changes to stale bytes; reads now happen inside the critical section for update, comment, and close. Lock-guard sabotage verified: releasing the lock immediately reproduces lost updates and fails the test. This evidence was originally appended in history events that precede the claim (the comment_add at 2026-08-22T11:40:19Z, the tests_add at 2026-08-27T00:43:58Z, and the files_add at 2026-08-27T00:43:58Z, all before the claim at 2026-08-27T00:44:42Z). It is restated here under established ownership rather than by rewriting the append-only, hash-chained history."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-27T20:19:46.699Z"}],"before_hash":"65d80a927e5fd7bf9caa22cd4059762b86a0e01a6ebb2fd1c3ef1b3349509e7d","after_hash":"3442c33eeb831d28143a3992a3fc3f298a1fcc3bec58a3c2a377d2e8b9c5b214","item_hash_version